/target
node_modules/
# === .handoff durability policy (ADR-0016 / HFTASK-0058) ===
# The kernel owns the canonical commit-vs-ignore taxonomy. The contents-form rules below are
# the durability fragment `hf gitignore` ships; `hf gitignore --check` / `hf doctor` fail-closed
# if a DURABLE path (tasks/, decisions/, loop/*.md, context/) is ever swallowed. Never add a
# bare `.handoff/` or `.claude/` ignore — Git can't re-include past an excluded parent dir.
# HFTASK-0035 (ADR-0004 §3.3/§6 rev): the local ledger is gitignored (legitimate per-repo
# source of record, never committed). `**` also covers the top-level path + grit worktrees.
.handoff/**/ledger.db
.handoff/**/*.db-wal
.handoff/**/*.db-shm
.handoff/**/*.rvf
/.handoff/packets/
/.handoff/workspaces/

.grit
/_workspace/
/_workspace_prev/

# HFTASK-0037: active.md is a derived view (hf renders it); like packets/, never committed.
/.handoff/active.md

# HFTASK-0048: the on-disk lock mirror is ephemeral advisory state (the ledger is
# authoritative); like the ledger.db, it is never committed.
/.handoff/locks/

# HFTASK-0021: delivery artifacts are generated from the authoritative ledger events
# (`.handoff/deliveries/<correlation_id>.delivery.json`). They are a front-door polling cache,
# not source truth, so they are never committed.
/.handoff/deliveries/
